      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nWhen users merge veNFTs using *VotingEscrow.merge()*, the source NFT is permanently burned without claiming or migrating accumulated bribes. This results in permanent loss of user funds because:\n\nThe source NFT is burned and ownerOf() returns address(0)\nUsers cannot claim bribes for burned tokens due to access control\nEven if access control was bypassed, bribes would be sent to address(0) and burned\n\n### Root Cause Analysis\n### 1: VotingEscrow.merge() Burns Source Without Claiming Bribes\nFile: ve33/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol \n```solidity\nfunction merge(uint _from, uint _to) external nonreentrant notPartnerNFT(_from) {\n    require(attachments[_from] == 0 && !voted[_from], \"ATT\");\n    require(_from != _to, \"SAME\");\n    require(_isApprovedOrOwner(msg.sender, _from) && \n            _isApprovedOrOwner(msg.sender, _to), \"NAO\");\n\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked0 = locked[_from];\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked1 = locked[_to];\n    require(_locked1.end > block.timestamp ||  _locked1.isPermanent,\"EXP||PERM\");\n    require(_locked0.isPermanent ? _locked1.isPermanent : true, \"!MERGE\");\n    \n    uint value0 = uint(int256(_locked0.amount));\n    uint end = _locked0.end >= _locked1.end ? _locked0.end : _locked1.end;\n\n    locked[_from] = IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false);\n    _checkpoint(_from, _locked0, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false));\n    _burn(_from);  // @audit BURNS SOURCE NFT WITHOUT CLAIMING BRIBES\n                   // @audit MISSING: Check for unclaimed bribes\n                   // @audit MISSING: Auto-claim before burn\n                   // @audit MISSING: Migration of bribe accounting\n\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory newLockedTo;\n    newLockedTo.isPermanent = _locked1.isPermanent;\n\n    if (newLockedTo.isPermanent){\n        newLockedTo.amount = _locked1.amount + _locked0.amount;\n        if (!_locked0.isPermanent) {\n            permanentLockBalance += value0;\n        }\n    }else{\n        newLockedTo.amount = _locked1.amount + _locked0.amount;\n        newLockedTo.end = end;\n    }\n\n    _checkpoint(_to, _locked1, newLockedTo);\n    locked[_to] = newLockedTo;\n\n    if(voted[_to]) {\n        IVoter(voter).poke(_to);\n    }\n    \n    emit Merge(msg.sender, _from, _to, uint(int256(_locked0.amount)), \n               uint(int256(_locked1.amount)), uint(int256(newLockedTo.amount)), \n               newLockedTo.end, block.timestamp);\n    // @audit No event or mechanism for bribe handling\n}\n```\nAfter _burn() is called:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _burn(uint _tokenId) internal {\n    require(_isApprovedOrOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId), \"NAO\");\n    address owner = ownerOf(_tokenId);\n\n    delete idToApprovals[_tokenId];\n    _removeTokenFrom(owner, _tokenId);\n    // @audit Above line sets: idToOwner[_tokenId] = address(0)\n    \n    VotingDelegationLib.moveTokenDelegates(cpData, delegates(owner), address(0), _tokenId, ownerOf);\n    emit Transfer(owner, address(0), _tokenId);\n}\n```\nResult: ownerOf(_tokenId) now returns address(0), making the NFT permanently inaccessible.\n\n### 2: VoterV3._reset() Does NOT Claim Bribes\nFile: ve33/contracts/VoterV3.sol \nUsers must ensure !voted[_from] before merging. They do this by calling reset():\n```solidity\nfunction _reset(uint256 _tokenId) internal {\n    address[] storage _poolVote = poolVote[_tokenId];\n    uint256 _poolVoteCnt = _poolVote.length;\n    uint256 _totalWeight = 0;\n\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < _poolVoteCnt; i ++) {\n        address _pool = _poolVote[i];\n        uint256 _votes = votes[_tokenId][_pool];\n\n        if (_votes != 0) {\n            weights[_pool] -= _votes;\n            votes[_tokenId][_pool] -= _votes;\n            \n            address internal_bribe = gaugeManager.fetchInternalBribeFromPool(_pool);\n            address external_bribe = gaugeManager.fetchExternalBribeFromPool(_pool);\n            \n            // @audit Only withdraws voting WEIGHT from bribe contracts\n            // @audit Does NOT claim accumulated rewards\n            IBribe(internal_bribe).withdraw(uint256(_votes), _tokenId);\n            IBribe(external_bribe).withdraw(uint256(_votes), _tokenId);\n\n            _totalWeight += _votes;\n            emit Abstained(_tokenId, _votes);\n        }\n    }\n    totalWeight -= _totalWeight;\n    usedWeights[_tokenId] = 0;\n    delete poolVote[_tokenId];\n    \n    // @audit CRITICAL: No bribe claiming occurs here\n    // @audit Unclaimed bribes remain in the bribe contracts\n}\n```\nResult: After reset(), voting weight is removed but unclaimed bribes still exist in the Bribe contracts, tied to the tokenId.\n\n### 3: GaugeManager.claimBribes() Fails for Burned Tokens\nFile: ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol \n```solidity\nfunction claimBribes(address[] memory _bribes, address[][] memory _tokens, uint256 _tokenId) external {\n    require(IVotingEscrow(_ve).isApprovedOrOwner(msg.sender, _tokenId), \"NAO\");\n    // @audit For burned NFT: ownerOf(_tokenId) = address(0)\n    // @audit isApprovedOrOwner returns FALSE\n    // @audit Transaction REVERTS with \"NAO\"\n    \n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < _bribes.length; i++) {\n        IBribe(_bribes[i]).getReward(_tokenId, _tokens[i]);\n    }\n}\n````\n\n### Why the check fails:\n\n VotingEscrow.sol - _isApprovedOrOwner()\n```solidity\nfunction _isApprovedOrOwner(address _spender, uint _tokenId) internal view returns (bool) {\n    address owner = idToOwner[_tokenId];  // @audit Returns address(0) for burned NFT\n    bool spenderIsOwner = owner == _spender;  // @audit false (address(0) != user)\n    bool spenderIsApproved = _spender == idToApprovals[_tokenId];  // @audit false (deleted in burn)\n    bool spenderIsApprovedForAll = (ownerToOperators[owner])[_spender];  // @audit false\n    return spenderIsOwner || spenderIsApproved || spenderIsApprovedForAll;\n    // @audit Returns FALSE → claimBribes reverts with \"NAO\"\n}\n```\n\n## IMPACT\nUsers  lose unclaimed bribes when merging veNFTs.\nEstimated loss ranges from $0 to $5,000+ per user, depending on accumulated rewards.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n – Auto-Claim Before Merge\n```solidity\nfunction merge(uint _from, uint _to) external nonReentrant {\n    _claimAllBribes(_from, msg.sender); // claim before burn\n    _burn(_from);\n    // continue merge logic...\n}\n```",
